# Input
```
-- The table is created after the index, so the index is on an existing table.
-- expect_lint/requireConcurrentIndexCreation
CREATE INDEX users_email_idx ON users (email);
CREATE TABLE users (id bigint, email text);

```

# Diagnostics
lint/requireConcurrentIndexCreation ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × Creating an index non-concurrently blocks writes to the table.
  
  i Use CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY to avoid blocking concurrent operations on the table.
